      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The quarter’s heart is Nikolaikirche, Berlin’s oldest church, originally a late Romanesque basilica erected around 1230.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikolaiviertel",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Ephraim‑Palais, built in 1766 for financier Veitel‑Heine Ephraim, was reconstructed 1983‑87 just 12 m from its original spot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikolaiviertel",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Knoblauchhaus, a neoclassical façade from 1760, now hosts a Biedermeier museum, Berlin’s oldest civic museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikolaiviertel",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The quarter once hosted a medieval trade route, the Mühlendamm ford, where the Spree could be crossed easily.",
